  <section>
    <h2>Winslow Dispensary Overview</h2>
    <p>Winslow is a Kennebec County town on the Kennebec River, directly across from Waterville. The two towns share a common economic and cultural identity, and the I-95 corridor that runs through them is the main north-south route through central Maine. Winslow's adult-use retail market is a single storefront (Daily Buds Dispensary) on China Rd, which serves the greater Waterville-Winslow area.</p>
    <p>Daily Buds is a Maine-grown multi-store brand. The Winslow location carries the full adult-use and medical menu — flower, pre-rolls, edibles, vapes, and concentrates — at Kennebec County pricing. For travelers on I-95, the Winslow storefront is a convenient central Maine stop.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Winslow</h2>
    <p>The table below lists the licensed adult-use storefront currently operating in Winslow. Hours, menus, and pricing change frequently — always verify directly with the operator before making the drive.</p>
    <table aria-label="Licensed dispensaries in Winslow, Maine">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Operator</th><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Website</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr><td>Daily Buds Dispensary LLC</td><td>10 China Rd Unit 2</td><td>https://www.dailybudsmaine.com/</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>All storefronts are licensed by the Maine Office of Cannabis Policy (OCP) for both adult-use and medical sales. Medical patients pay only the 5.5% state sales tax; adult-use customers pay the 10% state excise plus 5.5% sales tax on top of sticker price.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What to Expect on a First Visit</h2>
    <p>If you are 21 or older with a valid government-issued photo ID (Maine driver's license, out-of-state ID, or passport), you can walk into any adult-use dispensary in Winslow and purchase. The process is the same as buying alcohol — ID check at the door, browse the menu, transact at the counter, and walk out with a sealed exit bag.</p>
    <p>First-time visitors should expect a brief intake — the <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-staffing-licensing">budtender</a> will ask if you have used cannabis before, what effects you are looking for, and whether you have any preferences on format (flower, edible, vape, concentrate). Winslow's operator is used to serving both local regulars and I-95 travelers.</p>
    <p>For medical patients, bring your Maine medical cannabis card (or a valid out-of-state card if your state has a reciprocity agreement with Maine). Medical patients have access to higher-dose products and pay only the 5.5% state sales tax — a meaningful discount on larger purchases.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Pricing in Winslow</h2>
    <p>Pricing at Winslow dispensaries tracks the central Maine Kennebec County market, with the usual seasonal and competitive variation. As of mid-2026:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flower (eighth, 3.5g):</strong> $30-50, premium indoor can run higher</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-rolls (single 1g):</strong> $12-18, multi-packs $25-50</li>
      <li><strong>Edibles (100mg THC pack):</strong> $20-35, depending on format and brand</li>
      <li><strong>Distillate cartridges (1g):</strong> $35-50</li>
      <li><strong>Concentrates (1g):</strong> $40-80, depending on quality and format</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Medical patients save the 10% state excise — a meaningful discount on larger purchases. Adult-use customers should ask about first-time buyer promotions, birthday discounts, and weekday specials, which are common in this market.</p>
  </section>

